# RopeTest's full internal check suite; status 0 and every check "ok"
# confirms Rope.Mod's construction, Cat (incl. the short-leaf merge and
# absorb cases), Substring, Insert, Remove, Overwrite, Compare/Find/
# Repeat, the auto-rebalance / explicit Balance machinery, Head/Tail,
# and the newer additions (Map/Mapi, ASCII case, Trim, Escaped, char
# search, ContainsPattern, RFind, Blit, Iterate, Split, and the
# Iterator) all still behave as designed -- and the ones ported back
# from the Ada Ropes package later: IterateChunks, the linear Compare,
# Rider and whole-file I/O, the leaf-walking searches, character sets,
# FindToken, Count, Replace/ReplaceChar, Translate, mapped search,
# CompareString, case-insensitive comparison and Hash.
program RopeTest
status 0
output
ok - FromString of an empty string is NIL
ok - IsEmpty(NIL)
ok - ~IsEmpty(FromString(x))
ok - FromString/ToString round trip
ok - Length of FromString(hello)
ok - ToString(NIL) gives an empty string
ok - ToString truncates to fit, like ArgParser.String
ok - Length
ok - Fetch first character
ok - Fetch last character
ok - Length(NIL) = 0
ok - Cat(NIL, x) = x
ok - Cat(x, NIL) = x
ok - Cat of two short leaves: content
ok - Cat of two short leaves merges into one leaf
